1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,059
What if you doubled in size every two seconds?

2
00:00:03,099 --> 00:00:05,413
One moment you're brushing your teeth.

3
00:00:05,453 --> 00:00:08,386
Two seconds later your head touches the ceiling.

4
00:00:08,426 --> 00:00:11,111
Four seconds later, you're wearing the roof.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:15,368
By eight seconds you're taller than the apartments.

6
00:00:15,408 --> 00:00:17,988
Tiny people wave from the windows and the

7
00:00:18,028 --> 00:00:19,266
cars look like toys.

8
00:00:19,306 --> 00:00:22,588
Hypothetically, you should probably say sorry to the

9
00:00:22,628 --> 00:00:24,249
bakery you're standing on.

10
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,500
Sixteen seconds in, you're mountain-sized.

11
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:30,509
Clouds drift past your waist like fluffy sheep.

12
00:00:30,549 --> 00:00:32,750
A passing airplane buzzes your ear,

13
00:00:32,790 --> 00:00:35,568
and you politely resist the urge to swat it.

14
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:39,847
After forty-five seconds you're bigger than the whole planet.

15
00:00:39,887 --> 00:00:42,238
Earth sits in your palm like a marble.

16
00:00:42,278 --> 00:00:44,377
The Moon is small enough to flick,

17
00:00:44,417 --> 00:00:47,082
but a thought experiment says please don't.

18
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:50,876
In one minute you're as wide as the Sun.

19
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:53,634
Planets circle your fingers like beads on a

20
00:00:53,674 --> 00:00:56,071
string, and the Sun looks like a warm,

21
00:00:56,111 --> 00:00:57,803
friendly lamp in your hand.

22
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,047
By ninety seconds you're bigger than galaxies.

23
00:01:03,087 --> 00:01:04,897
Stars drift past like glitter.

24
00:01:04,937 --> 00:01:07,734
Physics says you'd collapse into a black hole,

25
00:01:07,774 --> 00:01:09,646
but in this thought experiment,

26
00:01:09,686 --> 00:01:10,941
you stay comfortable.

27
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:14,384
Soon the entire universe fits in your hands

28
00:01:14,424 --> 00:01:15,629
like a snow globe.

29
00:01:15,669 --> 00:01:18,534
Time stretches out, and for the first time

30
00:01:18,574 --> 00:01:20,471
all day you can finally say:

31
00:01:20,511 --> 00:01:22,823
I really needed that growth spurt.

32
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:27,576
Then you notice a tiny someone on your palm, waving.

33
00:01:27,616 --> 00:01:28,976
They're doubling too.

34
00:01:29,016 --> 00:01:30,175
And on their palm,

35
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:32,442
an even tinier someone waves back.

36
00:01:32,482 --> 00:01:34,841
It's growth spurts all the way down.
